.\" cartograph(1) — draft man page (Bloom UX). Render: man ./surveyor/cartograph.1
.TH CARTOGRAPH 1 "2026-06-17" "Cartograph 0.0" "Cartograph Manual"
.SH NAME
cartograph \- a living map of your machine's network, from orbit to the byte
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cartograph
.RI [ global-options ]
.RI [ verb ]
.RI [ target ]
.RI [ --lens
.IR list ]
.RI [ --since
.IR dur ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cartograph
shows, for every connection and packet on your machine,
.BR "what " "it is, " "who " "it is, " "where " "it goes, and " "why "
it was sent \(em with the local app's icon, the remote service's logo, a plain\(hylanguage
explanation, and a continuous zoom from "who is my machine talking to right now" all the
way down to raw packet bytes.
.PP
Run with no arguments it opens calmly into the
.B orbit
view (the living map) using the best available expression \(em the GTK app on a desktop,
the terminal UI otherwise. It then
.I blooms:
every step deeper is one discoverable keystroke or verb away. Observation is the default;
actions that change your system (deep capture, blocking) are always explicit.
.SH VERBS
.TP
.B orbit
Launch the living map (default). Force a frontend with \fB--gtk\fR or \fB--tui\fR.
.TP
.B watch
A fast, live, process\(hyattributed flow list in the terminal.
.TP
.B why \fItarget\fR
Explain a flow, host, or process in plain language: the originating process and its
parents, the destination's identity and geography, and the estimated impact \(em with the
reasons, never a black box. Try \fBcartograph why --me\fR for "what am I leaking now?"
.TP
.B peek \fIhost\fR
Print an identity/geo/risk "passport" card for a host.
.TP
.B trace \fIflow\fR
Deep\(hycapture a single flow (full payload) and optionally \fB--export\fR it to a
.B .pcap
for Wireshark.
.TP
.B block | allow | throttle \fIselector\fR
Apply an XDP firewall rule to an app, host, or flow. Use \fB--explain\fR / \fB--dry-run\fR
to preview the effect before it happens.
.TP
.B lens
List, toggle, and save information lenses and profiles (see \fBcartograph-lens\fR(7)).
.TP
.B ambient
A calm, always\(hyon visualization of your machine's network life.
.TP
.B replay \fB--since \fIdur\fR
Scrub back through past traffic, DVR style.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the environment and capabilities (kernel, BTF, privileges, GPU, deps).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -g ", " --gtk
Force the GTK expression.
.TP
.BR -t ", " --tui
Force the terminal expression.
.TP
.BR -l ", " --lens " \fIlist\fR"
Enable lenses, e.g. \fB--lens tls,geo,risk,gpu\fR. Prefix with \fB-\fR to drop one.
.TP
.BR -p ", " --profile " \fIname\fR"
Lens bundle: \fBcalm\fR, \fBnerd\fR, \fBsecurity\fR, \fBprivacy\fR, \fBresource\fR.
.TP
.BR -a ", " --app " \fIname\fR"
Scope to one application.
.TP
.BR -s ", " --since " \fIdur\fR"
Time window, e.g. \fB30m\fR, \fB1h\fR, \fBtoday\fR.
.TP
.B --no-fetch
Never fetch remote logos (maximum privacy; use cached/category glyphs only).
.TP
.B --theme " \fIname\fR"
\fBbloom\fR (default), \fBmono\fR, \fBmatrix\fR, \fBpaper\fR.
.TP
.BR -j ", " --json
Machine\(hyreadable output. \fB-P\fR/\fB--plain\fR for no color/glyphs.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
See your machine's outward life right now, calmly:
.PP
.RS
.B cartograph
.RE
.PP
"Why is chrome talking to that address?" \(em in English:
.PP
.RS
.B cartograph why pid:3983
.RE
.PP
What is this IP, and should I care?
.PP
.RS
.B cartograph peek 140.82.113.26
.RE
.PP
Capture one suspicious flow and open it in Wireshark:
.PP
.RS
.B cartograph trace flow:8a3f --export suspicious.pcap
.RE
.PP
Preview blocking a chatty telemetry daemon before doing it:
.PP
.RS
.B cartograph block app:telemetry-daemon --dry-run --explain
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/cartograph/
Profiles, saved lenses, named entities ("my NAS", "mom's VPN").
.TP
.I /run/cartograph.sock
Unix socket between the privileged \fBsurveyor\fR(8) daemon and the UI.
.SH SECURITY
The UI is unprivileged. Capture and blocking run in \fBsurveyor\fR(8), which holds only the
capabilities it needs (\fBcap_bpf\fR, \fBcap_perfmon\fR, \fBcap_net_raw\fR,
\fBcap_net_admin\fR) \(em never full root. Remote logo fetching is cached, rate\(hylimited,
opt\(hyin, and shown in your own map.
